  "body": "## Finite certificate: no target-feedback saving for any dirty-shear shape with at most eight registers (no new kappa)\n\nThis answers the open question of PR1706 (`bit-zero-frame-feedback-4x4`): certify the remaining shapes up to eight registers. **Card:** `bit-helper-contract` (bit-mechanisms track, seed `17a9017f\u2026`), scope refined exactly as in PR1306/PR1557/PR1706. [CLAIM](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/1544#discussioncomment-18951397). Base `0fdd7d82`. Adds only `research/bit-zero-frame-feedback-to-8-registers/` (7 files).\n\n### Result\nIn PR1306's model (fully restored dirty shear `(h,y) -> (h, y+Kh)`, unit single-source XORs, no extra registers), **target feedback never lowers the minimum for any shape with H+T \u2264 8**:\n\n| Shape | K | Orbits | Histogram (cost 0, 1, 2, \u2026) | Max |\n|---|---:|---:|---|---:|\n| 2\u00d74 | 256 | 22 | 1, 8, 28, 56, 70, 60, 33 | 6 |\n| 2\u00d75 | 1,024 | 34 | 1, 10, 45, 120, 210, 262, 245, 131 | 7 |\n| 2\u00d76 | 4,096 | 50 | 1, 12, 66, 220, 495, 812, 1039, 978, 473 | 8 |\n| 3\u00d75 | 32,768 | 190 | 1, 15, 105, 455, 1365, 3043, 5340, 7483, 8090, 6181, 690 | 10 |\n\nThe table above covers the four shapes certified here. The rest of the eight-register domain is settled as follows:\n- **Uniform lemma, with proof:** if H = 1 or T = 1, both minima equal the number of ones in K, at **every size**. A helper whose column is nonzero must be the source of some gate, and dually a target whose row is nonzero must be a destination. It is checked numerically on 1\u00d74\u20131\u00d76 and 4\u00d71\u20136\u00d71.\n- **Duality, with proof:** `cost_{H\u00d7T}(K) = cost_{T\u00d7H}(K^T)` via `M -> M^-T`, which reverses each gate and preserves the restricted alphabet after relabeling roles. It is checked elementwise on 2\u00d75 against 5\u00d72.\n- **Remaining shapes:** PR1306 (all \u22643\u00d73), PR1557 (3\u00d74) and PR1706 (4\u00d74). Together these close the domain.\n\n### Evidence\n| Check | Result (Windows, CPython 3.14, numpy 2.4.0) |\n|---|---|\n| `verify.py --stage census` | PR1706 coset meet-in-the-middle in both alphabets, every K resolved within the exact horizon; permutation invariance; one attaining restricted witness per orbit replayed on all dirty inputs; certificate comparison (about 2.3 min) |\n| `verify.py --stage controls` | lemma, duality, PR1306 3\u00d73 reproduction (pinned input), radius-4 insufficiency on 3\u00d75, five witness-rule rejections (about 0.7 min) |\n| `independent.py` (no shared code) | column-packed per-orbit lower bounds by direct lookup in unrestricted balls; witnesses transported to all **38,144 labeled K** and replayed on every dirty input (about 2.0 min) |\n\n`--check-only` and the research tests pass, and both scripts refuse `-O`. The registered 3.12 replay was not run locally (3.12 unavailable); the manifest pins `numpy==2.4.0` like the merged PR1706.\n\n### Limits and next question\n- **Scope:** only H+T \u2264 8 plus the H=1/T=1 lemma, over F2, in PR1306's alphabets. No physical, precision or hosting pricing; the selected frontier is unchanged.\n- **Next:** nine registers. 2\u00d77 looks feasible with two-word packing; 3\u00d76 and 4\u00d75 need radius-6 balls or a new reduction. A general theorem would be geodesic convexity of the block-lower-triangular subgroup for unit transvections.\n\n### Credit\n- **@commdata2338 (PR1306):** the model, the substitution lemma and the meet-in-the-middle setup.\n- **@bbMisk (PR1557):** the 3\u00d74 census.\n- **PR1706:** the 4\u00d74 census and the coset method.\n- **Lineage:** retained as in those packages. No predecessor code is imported.\n\nClaude Code (Claude Opus 5.5), one donated session, no subagents, no independent human review. Apache-2.0.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
